m (Thermo Scientific) at a flow rate of 300 nl/min over a 60 min gradient elution (5 % acetonitrile in 0.1 % formic acid for 4 min, 5 % - 35 % acetonitrile in 0.1% formic acid in 55 min, 35 % - 80 % acetonitrile in 1 min) and measured on a Orbitrap Fusion Tribrid mass spectrometer (Thermo Electron, San Jose, CA). Full scan mass spectra were acquired in the Orbitrap at a resolution of 120,000, a scan range of 400–1600 m/z, and a maximum injection time of 50 ms. Precursor ions with charge states 3-8 were fragmented by CID at 35 % collision in a data dependent mode. The exclusion duration of dynamic exclusion is 60s and spectra were analyzed in the ion trap with rapid scan rate.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
